    "description": "Handle manager commission, charity, equal portions, and other deductions before the remaining profit is shared.",
    "teachingApproach": "Use a two-layer envelope model: special allocation first, ordinary partnership second. Start with a manager's percentage, then charity, equal portions plus capital portions, and interest-style distributions. The working partner always gets the special amount plus the normal share unless the wording says otherwise. Questions deliberately include the trap of applying the capital ratio to the full profit before removing the special amount.",
